// A dormant seed with ground on top of it -- the seed bank. The same seed
// as `seed.ron` in every physical respect, with one difference: **it is not
// food** (`food_energy` 0), because a forager walking the surface does not
// find a seed that has sunk into the soil. Owner's ruling 2026-10-03 on the
// garden lane's card ("Make some fallen seed safe from ants so the garden
// keeps a stock?" -- *Build it*): in every played-bed garden the colony ate
// litter and seed faster than the plants replaced them, booming and then
// starving on a bare bed. Real harvester ants are seed predators *and*
// dispersers; the seeds they miss, buried ones above all, are what the
// plants come back from (MacMahon et al. 2000).
//
// Only `plant.rs` writes it, and only over a species' own `seed_material`
// (never `pip` or `windfall`): a seed whose cell above is ground becomes
// this, and turns back into its species' seed the tick it is uncovered.
// Germination does not read the material, so a buried seed sprouts on the
// same light and water rule as any other -- it only stops being eaten.
// On by default; `PIXEL_PHYSICS_BURIED_SEED=off` turns it off (see
// `plant::buried_seed_enabled` for the measurement).
(
    name: "buriedseed",
    display: "Buried seed",
    kind: Powder,
    density: 0.6,
    friction_angle: 55.0,
    // `seed.ron`'s palette, one shade darker: soil-stained, and only ever
    // seen in a cutaway.
    colors: [
        (108, 82, 44),
        (122, 94, 52),
        (94, 72, 38),
        (134, 104, 60),
    ],
    falls_through_organisms: true,
    flammability: 0.5,
    burn_temperature: 500.0,
    burn_duration: 30,
    burns_into: "ash",
    heat_conductivity: 0.15,
    food_energy: 0.0,
    penetration_resistance: 0.2,
)
